Subject: HWUI: skip a frame while the window has no surface instead of aborting

FLO (a music app) aborted in its RenderThread with "drawRenderNode called on a context with no
surface!" after the host's graphics renderer restarted. The recovery from a lost GPU device
destroys every window's surface and builds them again once the host GPU answers, and a frame
that came in between reached SkiaOpenGLPipeline::getFrame() (SkiaVulkanPipeline::getFrame() for
Vulkan), which aborts when the pipeline has no surface.

CanvasContext::draw() now skips such a frame, as it skips a frame while the device is lost, and
asks for the surface to be made again and the window to be drawn in full (onDeviceReset()). A
window that draws into a hardware buffer has no surface and is not skipped.

Applies on top of 0001 to frameworks/base (Android 16).
---
diff --git a/libs/hwui/renderthread/CanvasContext.cpp b/libs/hwui/renderthread/CanvasContext.cpp
--- a/libs/hwui/renderthread/CanvasContext.cpp
+++ b/libs/hwui/renderthread/CanvasContext.cpp
@@ -634,6 +634,12 @@
             return SkippedFrameReason::ContextIsStopped;
         }
 
+        if (!mHardwareBuffer && !mRenderPipeline->isSurfaceReady()) {
+            // The surface went with the lost device and is not made again yet: getFrame() aborts
+            // without one. The frame is skipped, and the surface and the window are made again.
+            return SkippedFrameReason::NoOutputTarget;
+        }
+
         if (!Properties::isDrawingEnabled()) {
             return SkippedFrameReason::DrawingOff;
         }
@@ -646,6 +652,10 @@
     }();
     if (skippedFrameReason) {
         mCurrentFrameInfo->setSkippedFrameReason(*skippedFrameReason);
+        if (*skippedFrameReason == SkippedFrameReason::NoOutputTarget) {
+            // Asks for the surface on the next frame callback and for a full redraw.
+            onDeviceReset();
+        }
 
 #ifdef __ANDROID__
         if (auto grContext = getGrContext()) {
